It has been argued that logic programming under well-founded model semantics can be understood as a logic of inductive definitions \cite{KR/DeneckerV14}. In this, \AFT's well-founded fixpoint construction constructs the relations inductively defined by the program. \citet{KR/DeneckerV14} claim that for such definitional programs, the well-founded model will always identify the defined set. In the application of \AFT for auto-epistemic logic (AEL), the well-founded fixpoint construction does not construct sets, but a belief state. 
