I-CSIT and QFC causes an offset which is not known by the receiver, and after several rounds of iteration, the offset is accumulated and cannot be eliminated in the receiver's decoding procedure, which leads to a decoding failure occurs. In Figure \ref{in3}, we show that applying a pair of modulo lattice function based encoder-decoder to the transceiver and introducing an auxiliary signal to the receiver's decoding procedure, the offset caused by I-CSIT and QFC only depends on the quantized noise which is known by the receiver, which indicates that this offset will not be accumulated and can be eliminated by the receiver, and hence the SK scheme still works in such a case.




