\begin{abstract}
In this paper, we outline a method to determine all recursive relations for a subnormal 2-variable weighted shift, up to total degree $k$, entirely from the representing measure. This allows us to show that the densities of the atoms do not affect the recursive relations. We then show that this method can be used to explicitly construct the Gröbner basis for the ideal of recursive relations.
\end{abstract}

