1 & 2 & 4 & 4 & 8 & 16 \\
1 & 3 & 2 & 9 & 6 & 4 \\
1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1
\end{bmatrix}$$

and 

$$\operatorname{ker}(V(\mu)(2))=\begin{bmatrix}
16 & 6 & -27 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\
12 & -8 & -9 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\
14 & -21 & 2 & 5 & 0 & 0
\end{bmatrix}.$$

Theorem 3.4 and $\operatorname{ker}(V(\mu)(2))$ imply that the recursive relations for $M(\mu)(2)$ are
