%\ee
%where $X'_{n+17} \ne X_{n+17}$. A measure of distance between $X'(t_n)$ and $X(t_n)$ can be defined in terms of the gravitational energy $E_G(X'(t_n), X(t_n))$ associated with the displacement of a single electron, say, by one Planck length. According to \cite{....}, for a solid ball of radius $R$ and mass $M$ displaced by a distance $b$, 
%\begin{align}
