In Fig.~\ref{fig2}(b), we plot the interlayer Ni-O-Ni bond angle $\alpha$ as a measure of the proximity towards the structural transition point from $Amam$ to $I4/mmm$ phase. The bond angle increases toward 180 degrees by reducing the lattice constant $a$, which is qualitatively consistent with a trend captured in a previous theoretical study~\cite{2505.12733}.
Within the present calculation scheme, however, the angle $\alpha$ does not reach 180 degrees even in the SLAO case. Nonetheless, we do not intend to conclude that the structure of the thin film on SLAO substrate has $Amam$ symmetry. In fact, for comparison, we also perform structural optimization assuming $I4/mmm$ symmetry and have found that the energy difference between $Amam$ and $I4/mmm$ phase is about few meV per unit cell, which is small. This suggests the difficulty in judging which phase is more stable between $Amam$ and $I4/mmm$ through first-principles calculations.
As mentioned in the Introduction, experiments suggest realization of $I4/mmm$ symmetry within the experimental error bar~\cite{2501.08204,QKXueThin}.


