Figure \ref{chemical_potential} shows the energy par particle for this system computed using the pair propagator for $g \in \{0.1, 0.5, 1.0\}$. For $g=0.1$, the energy par particle converges very quickly due to the weak interactions. The $1/N$ behaviour of $E/N$ suggests a linear model for the ground state energy as a function of $N$, 
\begin{equation}
