\subsubsection{Maximum likelihood degree of very affine varieties}

Theorem \ref{alg_deg_th} (2) follows directly from standard Lagrange multipliers techniques. Recall that the ML-degree is equal to the signed Euler characteristic.

\begin{theorem}\cite[Theorem 1]{Huh13}
    For a smooth very affine variety $U\subset (\Cc)^m$ and a generic character $\phi_u:(\Cc)^m \to \Cc, u \in \Z^m$ all critical points of $\phi_u$ on $U$ are non-degenerate and their number $\text{MLdeg}(U,u)$ is equal to the signed Euler characteristic $(-1)^{\dim U}\chi(U)$.
