Theorem \ref{alg_deg_th}(3) follows directly from standard Lagrange multipliers techniques. Recall that $\Ds_\rho$ is the support of the quadratic distance function  (containing the origin, all coordinate basis vectors, and their doubles). Denote by $E_i$ the $i$-th coordinate hyperplane in $\R^n$.

\begin{ex}(\cite{BSW22} and \cite{TT24})
    For Newton non-degenerate polynomials $f_1,\dots,f_m \in \C[z^{\pm 1}_1,\dots,z^{\pm 1}_{n-m}]$ all whose supports $\Ps_1,\dots,\Ps_m$ contain the origin $O$, the ED-degree of the complete intersection $V_{\mathbf f} = \{f_1 = {\dots} = f_m = 0\}$ is equal to:
