Consider the projection $\pi_2$ along the 3-space generated by $e_1,e_2,e_3$ to the 2-space generated by $e_5$ and $e_2+e_3+e_4$. The projection maps $P$ to the unit $2$-simplex. Thus, $P$ is isomorphic to the Cayley sum of two segments and a tetrahedron with vertices:

$$
\begin{pmatrix*}[r]
