	Additionally, we consider the weak blast wave problem for the ideal \ac{MHD} equations.
	Here, we employ a "1.5"-dimensional variant of the \ac{MHD} equations by enhancing the state vector by velocity and magnetic fields in $y$ and $z$ direction, while allowing variations only in $x$ direction.
	The divergence-free constraint of the magnetic field $\boldsymbol B$
	%
	\begin{equation}
		\label{eq:DivConstraint}
