Despite its strengths, HR-VILAGE-3K3M has limitations. It is currently restricted to human transcriptomics and lacks additional omics layers such as proteomics or genetic variants (e.g., SNPs), which would support comprehensive, multi-modal analyses. Additionally, while antibody measurements were curated where available, some studies did not report or release these data, limiting their utility for supervised outcome prediction. Future efforts may expand HR-VILAGE-3K3M to include murine models or integrate other data types to further enhance its utility. Overall, HR-VILAGE-3K3M fills a critical gap by offering a curated, ready-to-use dataset that promotes reproducible analysis, supports benchmarking of emerging methods, and accelerates discovery in systems immunology, particularly in infectious and immune disorders.

