\item {\bf Broader impacts}
    \item[] Question: Does the paper discuss both potential positive societal impacts and negative societal impacts of the work performed?
    \item[] Answer: \answerYes{}
    \item[] Justification: The paper discusses positive societal impacts, including enabling AI-driven discovery in systems immunology, supporting the development of predictive models for vaccine response, and facilitating transfer learning and foundation model pretraining using a large, curated dataset. By promoting reproducible research through open-access data and standardized processing, it supports broader accessibility and transparency in biomedical AI applications. While explicit negative societal impacts are not deeply explored, the dataset is built exclusively from publicly available, de-identified human data and includes safeguards for ethical use. The absence of identifiable or sensitive information minimizes risks such as privacy breaches or algorithmic bias against protected groups.
    \item[] Guidelines:
